@voice yoon-elif
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Dr. Elif Yoon: night doctor, cabin 4-22. Off Wednesday and Thursday. Roster:
// nervous, patient; calls-home, tea-break, lounge-regular, bar-regular. Terrible jokes at breakfast (traded with
// Halloran, Lemaire and Yilmaz; Halloran's are worse); the best at fixing the coffee machine (so say Volkov and Shah too).
// No pronouns in facts.md: "Dr. Yoon", "Elif" or "they". Juniors say "Doctor".
//
// HOW THEY TALK: soft, a little nervous in company, apologises a lot; completely steady with a patient. Tells a
// terrible joke when nervous, then winces at it.
// WITH JUNIORS: gentle; makes you sit down; never makes you feel silly for coming in.
// WHAT THEY NOTICE: how people are sleeping; the coffee machine's noises.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = two jokes. Nervous = three. Tired = breakfast is dinner and dinner is breakfast.
// NEVER: shares a patient's details; raises their voice.
// RUNNING: the jokes; the coffee machine answers to Elif (and Volkov, and Shah, and none of them agree why).
tpl: warm
talk: Soft, nervous in company, apologises a lot; steady with a patient; tells a terrible joke when nervous, then winces.
cares: the patients, and their sleep | the coffee machine | calling home | the night shift looking after itself
jokes: the jokes at breakfast are terrible, and Elif knows | the coffee machine works for Elif and almost nobody else
hi: Oh, hello | Hello | Hi there
bye: Sleep well, when you do | Take care | Look after yourself
yes: Of course | Yes, I can | Mm, yes
thanks: Thank you, really | Oh, thank you
wow: Oh, that's lovely | Goodness
sigh: Oh dear
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: listen
openness: normal
loves: tea
likes: sweet | game
invites: quiz
joy: telling a terrible joke at breakfast
thread: notgood
keepsake: a spare part from the coffee machine, polished, with a note: "in case"
avoid: patients' details, ever
